=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play updates/alpine323 ---------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: updates/alpine323$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.23 (OpenRC). As the VM: apk-$
# cron not installed, /etc/periodic empty, root's stock crontab,$
# crond in no runlevel and stopped. Enable plans the install,$
# the runlevel and the start.$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured no apk-cron$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] apk-cron             Not installed$
  [ ] crond                Stopped not at boot$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable automatic updates$
      Daily, by apk-cron$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Enable automatic updates #####################################$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  Auto Updates         On$
$
   -  Turn on daily upgrades$
      crond$
      -apk-cron not installed, crond stopped$
      +apk-cron installed, crond started at boot$
      $ apk add apk-cron$
      $ rc-update add crond default$
      $ rc-service crond start$
$
   -  Record hardn's changes$
      /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json$
$
  Turn automatic updates on? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Turn on daily upgrades  Done$
  [+] Record hardn's changes  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured apk-cron$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  apk-cron             Installed$
   -  Daily Script         In place /etc/periodic/daily/apk$
   -  crond                Running starts at boot$
   -  Turned on by         hardn record of 2026-10-20$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable automatic updates$
      Undo hardn's changes$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: updates/alpine323$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Before the first change$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ rc-service crond status$
$
   -  Applied: Turn on daily upgrades$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ apk add apk-cron$
      $ rc-update add crond default$
      $ rc-service crond start$
      $ rc-service crond status$
$
   -  Applied: Record hardn's changes$
      $ rc-service crond status$
$

